The files cpu.py, families.py, model.py, probe.py and scan.py are copied without
source changes from this commit. TUI, authentication, inventory discovery,
notifications and AI integration are not included.

FL dashboard integration changes live in fl_dashboard/resources/telemetry.py:
- Use existing dashboard SSH profiles instead of separate JumpServer credentials.
- Correct timeout shell assignment, require timeout, and cap the entire probe.
- Correct node uptime ordering and CPU idle+iowait fields in the generated probe.
- Reject every unsuccessful summary query, preserve MetaX/Enflame process query status,
  require positive process evidence, and mark every truncated vendor table unknown.
- Treat ambiguous memory capacity and unassigned Hygon queues conservatively.
- Omit login/top-process collection and command-line reads; Hygon uses comm.
- Add completion checking and reject incomplete, malformed or stalled availability.
- Bound and sanitize UI fields, preserve chip/board counts, and compute CPU deltas.
- Repair Ascend board/process ownership from explicit NPU numbers in repeated headers.
- Do not infer free accelerator capacity when no supported tool answers.

Parser test snippets in tests/test_device_telemetry.py are minimized and anonymized
adaptations of upstream parser fixtures, under the same Apache-2.0 license.
